    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today with our heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** all sidelined by team off-days. In their absence, **Nasim Nunez** emerges as our strongest play of the day with a 64.14 efficiency score. While he is currently projected at the #8 spot, his matchup against the vulnerable Ryan Feltner (5.10 xERA) provides a massive 19% boost in SP skill, and his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in a league where stolen bases are the scarcest commodity. Following him is **Sam Antonacci** (59.34), who benefits from a prime lead-off role against Kumar Rocker, buoyed by a 10% order bonus and favorable platoon dynamics.\n\nOur remaining core carries a high floor, but we are keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks** (49.04), whose status as a left-handed bat facing the veteran Framber Valdez leads to a significant 11% platoon penalty. While **Tommy White** (55.05) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.64) present steady options, they are tethered to \"Lineup Pending\" designations; should any of these players move down in the order or face late defensive replacements, their marginal scores could dip further. **Jackson Merrill** (51.55) rounds out the outfield despite a challenging matchup against Braxton Ashcraft, as his 13% dynamic platoon edge narrowly justifies his inclusion over the remainder of the bench. We are managing the roster carefully today, cognizant that with elite talent like **Jordan Westburg**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Coby Mayo** unavailable due to the team-wide scheduling void, we must rely on the stolen base upside of players like **Nasim Nunez** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
